<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner in 20 mln stg Egyptian deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner in 20 mln stg Egyptian deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian industrial group Kvaerner ASA said on Friday that Kvaerner John Brown had signed a contract with Egypt's Nasr Petroleum Company (NPC) to help build a new hydro-cracker plant at NPC's Suez Refinery.</p>
<p>The five-year contract is worth 20 million pounds, Kvaerner said in a statement to the Oslo Stock Exchange.</p>
